<title>JAPAN: Japan May beef imports down 20 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May beef imports down 20 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in May totalled 45,877 tonnes, down by 20 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    May 97	 Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p> Total	    45,877	 77,370     57,382</p>
<p> Refrigerated   27,661	 30,058     22,901</p>
<p> Frozen	   18,216	 47,312     34,481</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     14,764	 17,660     13,261</p>
<p>  U.S.	    11,928	 11,474	8,932</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     May 97	 Apr 97     May 96</p>
<p>  U.S.	     9,042	 27,852     20,163</p>
<p>  Australia	7,410	  6,066     10,721</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first five months of 1997 were 129,939 tonnes against 115,676 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the January-May period of this year were 108,734 tonnes against 149,104 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
